  "headline": "Syria's Foreign Ministry condemns Houthi drone attack on Medina power station",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Syria’s Foreign Ministry condemned a Houthi drone attack on a power distribution station in Medina, Saudi Arabia, on Friday. According to the North Press Agency, the ministry stated the strike targeted civilian infrastructure. The ministry further asserted that the attack on the station, which provides electricity to the Prophet’s Mosque, violated Saudi Arabia’s sovereignty and threatened regional stability."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Government intervention begins at Mallam Junction to address recurring flooding",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Renewed government intervention at Mallam Junction in Ghana is underway to address landfill, drainage, and environmental challenges linked to recurring flooding in the area. According to MyJoyOnline, the efforts aim to provide a lasting solution for local residents, motorists, and businesses. The initiative follows engagements initiated from Jubilee House under Chief of Staff Julius Debrah, which involved the Weija-Gbawe Municipal Assembly, relevant government agencies, and private-sector stakeholders to focus on blocked drainage channels and landfill issues surrounding the junction. This activity is part of broader government efforts to restore waterways and drainage systems in flood-prone areas across Greater Accra. The Post-Flood Mitigation Task Force is coordinating the exercise with the stated objective of restoring waterway integrity and reducing flooding impacts in affected communities."
    },
    {
      "text": "In August, work commenced to reclaim the Lafa water retention basin at Mallam. The 48 Engineer Regiment of the Ghana Armed Forces was deployed to remove years of accumulated silt and solid waste that had reduced the basin's capacity to retain stormwater. The operation also included the removal of illegal structures and includes plans to construct protective embankments. Local residents and businesses have expressed hope that the sustained government presence at drainage and landfill sites represents a departure from previous interventions that typically intensified only after heavy rainfall. The involvement of the Weija-Gbawe Municipal Assembly is noted as critical for local sanitation enforcement, drainage maintenance, and monitoring activities around the affected areas."
    }
  ]
}

